SUMMARY:It Was Just An Accident
DTSTART:20251124T234500Z
DTEND:20251125T014500Z
DTSTAMP:20251124T234500Z
UID:vv4W2mxfcw
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 105 mins (1h45m)\n\nWinner of this year’s Palme d
 ’Or at Cannes\, the latest from Iranian auteur Jafar Panahi — his firs
 t following his most recent prison sentence — follows a group of citizen
 s pondering revenge against a man they believe was their torturer. Jafar P
 anahi scheduled to attend November 20 6:45pm screening.\n\nhttps://www.sif
 f.net/cinema/in-theaters/it-was-just-an-accident\n\nEstimated start: 16:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seattle 48 Hour Film Project Horror Awards 2025
DTSTART:20251125T030000Z
DTEND:20251125T054500Z
DTSTAMP:20251125T030000Z
UID:se29lgAsoi
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 150 mins (2h30m)\n\nPresented by Create 48 Media Ne
 twork and Seattle 48 Hour Film Project The Seattle 48 Hour Horror Film Pro
 ject is an annual competition where filmmakers have just one weekend to wr
 ite\, shoot\, and edit a short horror film. The event highlights Washingto
 n’s vibrant film community now in its 20th year. This is a screening of 
 a selection of our Award Winners and audience favorites\, followed by our 
 awards ceremony!\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/seattle-48-hou
 r-film-project-horror-screening-and-awards-ceremony-2025\n\nEstimated star
 t: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
